The chance of a level-drain attack succeeding is a base 33%, assuming it
even hits.  MC=3 multiplies that chance by 0.02.  In other words, even
if the attack physically hits, the chance of it draining you if you're
wearing proper armor, which you should be by the quest, is 0.66%.  One
out of every 150 attacks.  

Outside of the quest, you probably won't even have to deal with that
many level-draining attacks.  And once you're on the quest, XL is only
of marginal importance anyway, so on the off-chance you get drained,
it's no big deal.  

A resistance that only has a small chance of being useful even once a
game isn't worth the severe drop in damage you get when you use stormy.

